meta {
  name: 9f. Toggle openDataAccess → true (triggers UPDATE saga)
  type: http
  seq: 27
  tags: [
    requires-nifi
  ]
}

put {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/datasets/:id/released/meta
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

params:path {
  id: {{sagaDataSetId}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "name": "Saga Test DataSet",
    "description": "Dataset for end-to-end saga workflow test",
    "openDataAccess": true
  }
}

script:pre-request {
  // The CREATE saga (step 8) must have fully settled before we can update released meta,
  // otherwise the backend returns 409 (saga in-flight). Poll pendingSagaType until null.
  // assignments/namedApis are intentionally omitted from the body: per DataSetInputDTO the
  // null reconciler leaves those collections untouched (so step 10 assignments survive).
  // NOTE: Bruno's QuickJS sandbox lacks URLSearchParams and does not honour a validateStatus
  // function across the VM boundary, so we build the form body as a string and use try/catch.
  const axios = require('axios');
  const base = bru.getEnvVar('baseUrl');
  const kc = bru.getEnvVar('keycloakUrl');
  const realm = bru.getEnvVar('realm');
  const id = bru.getVar('sagaDataSetId');

  const form =
    'grant_type=password' +
    '&client_id=' + encodeURIComponent(bru.getEnvVar('clientId')) +
    '&client_secret=' + encodeURIComponent(bru.getEnvVar('clientSecret')) +
    '&username=' + encodeURIComponent(bru.getEnvVar('username')) +
    '&password=' + encodeURIComponent(bru.getEnvVar('password'));

  let bearer = '';
  try {
    const tok = await axios.post(`${kc}/realms/${realm}/protocol/openid-connect/token`, form, {
      headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/x-www-form-urlencoded' },
    });
    bearer = tok.data && tok.data.access_token;
  } catch (e) { /* token fetch failed; the PUT below will surface a clear error */ }

  for (let i = 0; i < 30; i++) {
    let pending = 'unknown';
    try {
      const r = await axios.get(`${base}/datasets/${id}`, { headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${bearer}` } });
      pending = r.data.pendingSagaType;
    } catch (e) { /* transient; retry */ }
    if (pending === null || pending === undefined) break;
    await new Promise(res => setTimeout(res, 2000));
  }
}

tests {
  test("openDataAccess update accepted (200)", function() {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });

  test("Dataset now reports openDataAccess=true", function() {
    expect(res.body.openDataAccess).to.equal(true);
  });
}

docs {
  **Saga step 9f of 18** — Flip a released dataset to open data access (issue #1368, journey J3).

  `PUT /datasets/{id}/released/meta` with `openDataAccess: true` updates the released dataset and triggers a **DATASET_UPDATE** saga that re-applies the FROST project `public` flag and **removes** the APISIX auth plugin from the dataset's route. `assignments` and `namedApis` are omitted so the null reconciler leaves them untouched (keeps step 10 green; named APIs are immutable while released anyway).

  **Precondition:** CREATE saga (step 8) has settled (`pendingSagaType == null`, polled in pre-request); dataset is AVAILABLE.

  **Expected Response:** 200 OK, body `openDataAccess: true`. The UPDATE saga then reconciles the route to open (verified in 9g).
}
